  "interpretation": [
    "The two complete-output acquisition samples are 192.716169667 s at T32 and 193.08759675 s at T100. These two shapes do not establish an asymptotic law or timing variability.",
    "T32 output selection removes beliefs and other State payloads as well as centered learning outputs. Output bytes fall 95.19%, acquisition time is 3.73% longer, temporary bytes rise 2.67%, and process high-water is 0.81% lower. With one sample per variant, this does not establish a reliable compilation-cost saving or isolate learning/recovery-specific cost.",
    "All numerical argument, fixed-metadata, output-descriptor and inspected StableHLO floating types were native float32 with x64 disabled and explicit x64 rejected. No runtime internal arrays, terminal certificates or solver results were observed.",
    "All persistent and auxiliary XLA caches were disabled; each process recorded zero persistent hit/miss log events and 144 tracing misses including layout setup. The zero persistent log counts are not cold-backend proof. Each complete program had one lower call, one compile call and zero executable calls.",
    "Process wait4 high-water covers the whole child lifetime, including compilation; XLA estimates describe executable storage, not compiler RSS. The backend-specific peak_memory_in_bytes field has limited semantics and is not used as the process peak.",
    "Current unbound D12 already holds parameters fixed. No recovery fit or parameter-update loop is compiled here. Physical learning-coordinate conversion, export and recovery fits are absent from both compared programs; learning-array finiteness remains an inference/status dependency.",
    "Production compiler/Engine remains D9; ordinary existing users do not compile this unbound D12 solver. Future public activation remains explicit. Compatible shapes/dtypes/static layouts may reuse executables, but no cross-process reuse or execution amortization was measured.",
    "Proceed to the reviewed moderate harness after the suite-margin prerequisite. Retain compatible executables across its authorized starts; keep full required learning outputs and all failure checks. Measure synchronized moderate execution time before claiming amortization or recovery cost/benefit. The registered three-fit recovery gate remains unchanged and recovery quality is not established."
